# Svelte and the options UI

Svelte is used for the extension's own pages — options, popup, targets, ToS — never for content injected into Torn
pages. DOM work on torn.com uses the helpers in `@common/utils`.

## Svelte 5 only

Runes throughout. No legacy syntax; `svelte-check` runs as a PR gate.

- `$props()` with a typed `interface` for props, `$bindable()` for two-way values like `ref` and `checked`.
- `$state()`, `$derived()` / `$derived.by()`, `$effect()`.
- Snippets and `{@render children?.()}` — no `<slot>`, no `export let`, no `createEventDispatcher`.
- Always `<script lang="ts">`.
- `PascalCase.svelte` filenames everywhere except inside `components/ui/`, which keeps shadcn's kebab-case.
- Cross-page state lives in `*.svelte.ts` stores (see `stores/database-store.svelte.ts`); component-local state stays in
  `$state`.

## The `ui/` folder is vendored

`src/extension/svelte/components/ui/` is generated by shadcn-svelte — `nova` style, `zinc` base colour, phosphor icons,
per [components.json](mdc:components.json). Treat it as a dependency:

- Compose the existing primitives instead of hand-rolling switches, dialogs, tables or tooltips. There are ~31 of them:
  accordion, alert, alert-dialog, badge, button, button-group, card, checkbox, collapsible, command, data-table, dialog,
  field, hover-card, input, input-group, kbd, label, popover, radio-group, scroll-area, select, separator, slider,
  sonner, spinner, switch, table, textarea, toggle, tooltip.
- Add new primitives with the CLI (`bunx shadcn-svelte@latest add <component>`), not by hand.
- Don't casually edit files in `ui/`; upstream updates overwrite them. Deliberate customisations belong in the sibling
  `helper.ts` variant definitions.
- Import through the barrels: `import { Button } from "@svelte/components/ui/button"` or
  `import * as Field from "@svelte/components/ui/field"`.

Application-level components live next to the entrypoint that uses them
(`src/extension/entrypoints/options/components/...`), not in `@svelte/components/ui`.

## Styling

- Tailwind 4, configured through `@theme` in `src/extension/svelte/app.css`. Use the semantic tokens (`bg-background`,
  `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`) rather than raw palette colours.
- Merge classes with `cn()` from `@svelte/utils`, and always let callers override via a `class` prop:
  `class={cn("rounded-md border", className)}`.
- Variants go in a sibling `helper.ts` using `tailwind-variants` (`tv({ base, variants, defaultVariants })`), not inline
  conditionals scattered through the markup.
- Oxfmt sorts Tailwind classes; don't fight the ordering.
- Theme switching uses `mode-watcher` (`ModeWatcher`, `setMode()`) driven by `settings.themes.pages`. The `.dark` class
  applies to extension pages only — Torn pages use Torn's own `body.dark-mode`, and those colours come from
  `globalVariables.css`.

## Icons

`phosphor-svelte`, imported per icon: `import TrashIcon from "phosphor-svelte/lib/Trash"`. Content scripts must instead
use the SVG factories in `@common/utils/icons/phosphor-icons` — never import `phosphor-svelte` outside Svelte pages.

## Adding a setting to the options UI

1. **Default** — declare it in `DEFAULT_STORAGE` in `src/common/utils/data/default-database.ts`. The
   `PreferenceStoragePath` types derive from it, so TypeScript will reject a path you haven't declared.
2. **Control** — add it to the matching `*Section.svelte` under
   `src/extension/entrypoints/options/components/preferences/`, using `StorageSwitch`, `StorageNumber`, `StorageSelect`
   or `StorageText`. They read and write storage themselves; don't wire up your own handler.

   ```svelte
   <PreferenceSectionCard title="Gym">
       <PreferenceSettingGroup>
           <StorageSwitch path="settings.pages.gym.progress" label="Display estimated gym energy progress" />
           <StorageSwitch path="settings.pages.gym.graph" label="Display stat graph" externalServices={["tornstats"]} />
       </PreferenceSettingGroup>
   </PreferenceSectionCard>
   ```

   Pass `externalServices` for anything depending on a third-party service — it disables the control and renders the
   requirement badge automatically. Nest dependent sub-settings as `children` of the parent switch.
3. **Search** — add a `PREFERENCE_SEARCH_DATA` entry in `preference-search-data.ts` with matching `path`, `label`,
   `group` and `section`. Keywords must not repeat the label or the last path segment; check with
   `bun run tools/validate-preference-keywords.ts`.
4. **New section or group** — register it in `PREFERENCE_GROUPS` in `configuration.ts`, create the `*Section.svelte`,
   and add the branch to the group's `*Group.svelte` dispatch (and `PreferencesContent.svelte` for a whole new group).

Routing is `svelte-spa-router` with `/preferences/{group}/{section}`; the navigation is generated from
`PREFERENCE_GROUPS`, so there is nothing to wire by hand once the configuration entry exists.

## Talking to the background

Use the proxies — `BACKGROUND_SERVICE` and `SOURCE_SERVICE` from `@extension/services/proxy-services` — for
notifications, forced data updates, cache operations and alarm resets. Never re-implement background logic in a page,
and never call `browser.storage` directly; go through `ttStorage`.
